  "question": {
    "text": "The dimensions of a cone are measured using a scale with a least count of $2 \\mathrm{~mm}$. The diameter of the base and the height are both measured to be $20.0 \\mathrm{~cm}$. The maximum percentage error in the determination of the volume is _______ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": 3,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/QMyMlsC7bx2Hqzr6BA5DakVMNgnT1DYjAMskB0b3FFE.original.fullsize.png\">\n$\\mathrm{V}=\\frac{1}{3} \\pi\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{D}}{2}\\right)^2 \\mathrm{H}$\n$\\therefore \\%$ Error in $\\mathrm{V}=2$ (% error in $\\mathrm{D})+\\%$ error in $\\mathrm{H}$.\n$\\because$ Least count is $2 \\mathrm{~mm}$.\n$\\therefore \\%$ error in D $=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~mm}}{20 \\mathrm{~cm}} \\times 100 \\%=1 \\%$\n& % error in $\\mathrm{H}=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~mm}}{20 \\mathrm{~cm}} \\times 100 \\%=1 \\%$\nSo $\\%$ error in $\\mathrm{V}=2 \\times 1 \\%+1 \\%=3 \\%$",
    "image": null
  },
